# Events Structured Reference

This file reorganizes event knowledge into the same keyed mechanic format used by other deterministic knowledge sources.
The original raw source remains preserved in public/knowledge/events for side-by-side comparison.

Mechanic: Events
Type: System
Domain: Limited-Time Progression
Section: Events
Category: Progression
Aliases: none.
Definition: Events are repeating challenge cycles that reward medals for completing mission tiers.
Behavior:
Events unlock in Milestones at Tier 1 Wave 70.
Events run on a repeating two-week cadence.
Event progress centers on missions, medal rewards, relic thresholds, and the event shop.

Mechanic: Event Cycle
Type: Schedule Rule
Domain: Events
Section: Events
Category: Schedule
Aliases: event rotation; event cadence
Definition: Event Cycle is the repeating two-week schedule that controls mission rollout and event downtime.
Behavior:
Each event lasts 2 weeks.
The first 8 days add new missions.
The final 6 days add no new missions.
When one event ends, the next event starts immediately.

Mechanic: Event Missions
Type: Objective System
Domain: Events
Section: Events
Category: Missions
Aliases: missions; event quests
Definition: Event Missions are the challenge list that awards medals during an event.
Behavior:
All event missions have 3 tiers.
Higher tiers ask for larger requirements and give larger medal payouts.
Missions remain available until the current event ends.
Mission categories can draw from always-available tasks, base combat goals, workshop actions, cards, labs, and ultimate weapons.

Mechanic: Event Mission Tiers
Type: Reward Table
Domain: Events
Section: Events
Category: Missions
Aliases: mission tier rewards
Definition: Event Mission Tiers are the three medal-paying completion levels attached to each event mission.
Behavior:
Tier 1 rewards 10 medals.
Tier 2 rewards 15 medals.
Tier 3 rewards 20 medals.
Each higher tier requires more progress than the previous tier.

Mechanic: Event Mission Rollout
Type: Availability Rule
Domain: Events
Section: Events
Category: Missions
Aliases: mission unlock schedule
Definition: Event Mission Rollout controls how many new missions appear during the first part of an event.
Behavior:
7 missions are available on the first day.
2 more missions are added each day for the next 7 days.
No new missions appear during the final 6 days of the event.

Mechanic: Event Rewards
Type: Reward System
Domain: Events
Section: Events
Category: Rewards
Aliases: medal rewards
Definition: Event Rewards are the medals and relic-threshold progress earned by completing event missions.
Behavior:
Completing mission tiers awards medals.
Collected medals also count toward event relic thresholds when those medals were earned during the current event.
Medals do not need to be spent to claim earned relic thresholds.

Mechanic: Event Booster
Type: Premium Modifier
Domain: Events
Section: Events
Category: Rewards
Aliases: booster; event pass booster
Definition: Event Booster doubles medal rewards for the event in which it is purchased.
Behavior:
The event booster doubles medal amounts for that event only.
Booster-doubled medals also count toward relic thresholds.
A booster must be purchased separately for each event where doubled medals are wanted.

Mechanic: Event Relic Progress
Type: Threshold System
Domain: Events
Section: Events
Category: Rewards
Aliases: relic thresholds; event relic milestones
Definition: Event Relic Progress is the medal-earned threshold track that unlocks event relic rewards.
Behavior:
350 medals unlock the first rare relic.
550 medals unlock the first premium rare relic.
700 medals unlock the second epic relic.
1100 medals unlock the second premium epic relic.
Medals carried over from previous events or earned from daily mission boxes do not count toward this progress.

Mechanic: Event Shop
Type: Store
Domain: Event Store
Section: Events
Category: Purchases
Aliases: event store
Definition: Event Shop is the medal-spending store that remains available even when no event is active.
Behavior:
The event shop spends medals.
The shop remains open even while no event is running.
The shop offers currencies, themes, relics, songs, and bots.

Mechanic: Event Shop Currency Purchases
Type: Cost Ladder
Domain: Medals
Section: Events
Category: Purchases
Aliases: event exchange; event currency costs
Definition: Event Shop Currency Purchases are the medal exchange options and scaling price ladder for currencies in the event shop.
Behavior:
Each exchange gives either 150 gems, 15 stones, or 250 shards.
There are four shard types tied to the four module families.
Buying shards increases the cost of the other shard types as well.
Costs:
Purchase 1 costs 40 medals.
Purchase 2 costs 65 medals.
Purchase 3 costs 90 medals.
Purchase 4 costs 130 medals.
Purchase 5 costs 175 medals.
Purchase 6 costs 230 medals.
Purchase 7 costs 380 medals.

Mechanic: Event Themes
Type: Cosmetic Rotation
Domain: Event Store
Section: Events
Category: Purchases
Aliases: event themes
Definition: Event Themes are rotating event-shop cosmetics that remain permanently unlocked once purchased.
Behavior:
Themes rotate each event and can be missed.
One tower theme costs 150 medals.
One background theme costs 250 medals.
Purchased event themes remain available forever.

Mechanic: Event Relics
Type: Limited Purchase
Domain: Event Store
Section: Events
Category: Purchases
Aliases: event store relics
Definition: Event Relics are limited medal purchases sold in the event shop and distinct from the relics earned through medal thresholds.
Behavior:
Event-shop relics are sold at 200-medal and 500-medal price points.
These relics can be limited to the sponsoring event.
Earned event relics and purchased event relics are separate acquisition paths.

Mechanic: Event Songs
Type: Permanent Purchase
Domain: Event Store
Section: Events
Category: Purchases
Aliases: songs
Definition: Event Songs are fixed event-shop purchases that each grant a permanent coin bonus.
Behavior:
There are 3 songs available.
Songs do not rotate.
Each song costs 200 medals.
Each song grants a +0.6% coin bonus.

Mechanic: Event Store Bots
Type: Store Category
Domain: Event Store
Section: Events
Category: Purchases
Aliases: bot shop; event bots
Definition: Event Store Bots are the bot unlocks sold through the event shop for medals.
Behavior:
Bots are purchased only with medals in the event shop.
The shop offers Flame, Thunder, Golden, and Amplify bots.
Purchased bots do not reset between events.
Bots can be toggled on or off in the shop between rounds.

Mechanic: Event Bot Unlock Costs
Type: Cost Ladder
Domain: Medals
Section: Events
Category: Purchases
Aliases: bot unlock ladder
Definition: Event Bot Unlock Costs are the escalating medal costs for unlocking additional bots from the event shop.
Behavior:
The first bot costs 150 medals.
The second bot costs 300 medals.
The third bot costs 600 medals.
The fourth bot costs 900 medals.
Each additional unlocked bot raises the cost of the next bot unlock.

Mechanic: Bot Respec
Type: Reset Rule
Domain: Event Store
Section: Events
Category: Purchases
Aliases: event bot respec
Definition: Bot Respec refunds medal-based bot unlocks and medal-based bot upgrades for a gem fee once per event.
Behavior:
Bot respec costs 300 gems.
Bot respec is available once per event.
Bot labs are not refunded by bot respec.
Only medal-related bot unlocks and medal-related bot upgrades are refunded.
